Hi everyone,


I'm wondering if anyone has gotten stuck on the find.clusters function?


I did a DAPC on this exact dataset in some months back and now I want that I redo it to check a different K value and change the colours, but it keeps getting stuck on find.clusters.


Any idea what may be causing this? If I remember correctly, this step doesn't take long, definitely not more than a day.


I've tried on a new mac and also on a PC using the parallel = FALSE argument.

Any help is appreciated.

>pldata = read.PLINK("batch_1_recode.raw")

>grp = find.clusters(pldata, max.n.clust = 15)         ##GETS  STUCK ON THIS



